        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Excuse My French, Pop That\n- People: Machine Gun Kelly, Richard Colson Baker, MGK, Diddy, Nicki Minaj, Drake, Ace Hood, Lil Wayne, Birdman, The Weeknd, Rick Ross, 2 Chainz, Max B, Ne-Yo, Raekwon, Scarface, Snoop Dogg\n- Places: Cleveland, Ohio\n- Topics: guest appearances, stage names, music career\n\nFacts:\n- In 2006, Machine Gun Kelly began his music career as a teenager by releasing a mixtape.\n- Richard Colson Baker was born on April 22, 1990, and he is an American rapper and actor from Cleveland, Ohio who is better known as MGK or Machine Gun Kelly.\n- Pop That was released as the first single from the 2013 debut studio album Excuse My French.\n- Pop That features guest appearances from Rick Ross, Drake, and Lil Wayne.\n- Excuse My French features guest appearances from Diddy, Nicki Minaj, Drake, Ace Hood, Lil Wayne, Birdman, The Weeknd, Rick Ross, 2 Chainz, Max B, Ne-Yo, Machine Gun Kelly, Raekwon, Scarface, and Snoop Dogg.",
